Release	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-06T18:13:41.0553333Z [{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-foundation/browser-commander/pulls/127","id":4761778251,"node_id":"PR_kwDOQYTTi88AAAABG9L4Sw","html_url":"https://github.com/link-foundation/browser-commander/pull/127","diff_url":"https://github.com/link-foundation/browser-commander/pull/127.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/link-foundation/browser-commander/pull/127.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-foundation/browser-commander/issues/127","number":127,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"feat: add native Safari and Technology Preview WebDriver control","user":{"login":"konard","id":1431904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1431904?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard","html_url":"https://github.com/konard","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Safari and Technology Preview were listed as import sources, but `launchRealBrowser({ channel: 'safari' })` rejected them and the catalogue had no driver path. This adds native W3C WebDriver control in JavaScript, Python and Rust, including common launchers and the shared CLI.\n\n- Use the installed Safari/Technology Preview driver, without creating a persistent profile. Support navigation, find/click/fill, sync/async evaluation, screenshots, cookies, windows and tabs through the existing adapters and native handles.\n- Recognize Remote Automation and driver authorization failures, preserve diagnostics, explain the one-time settings and `safaridriver --enable` steps, and expose an explicit settings opener. Library code never enables automation automatically.\n- Seed imported cookies per domain, restore portable cookies/localStorage, and document Safari's isolated ephemeral sessions. Network interception, tracing and PDF return typed unsupported errors.\n- Update the shared catalogue, generated support/parity tables, setup documentation and all three release fragments. Update transitive `shell-quote` to 1.12.0 to resolve the critical audit finding in the initial PR security run.\n\nFixes #126.\n\n## Reproduction and validation\n\nReproduce the original failure on macOS with `await launchRealBrowser({ channel: 'safari' })`: the previous launcher rejects Safari as a non-CDP browser. Catalogue regressions also failed before implementation because `controlProtocol` was null and driver executables were absent.\n\nRegression coverage:\n\n```sh\n(cd js && node --test tests/unit/browser/safari.test.js tests/unit/browser/webdriver.test.js)\n(cd python && pytest tests/unit/browser/test_safari_webdriver.py)\n(cd rust && cargo test --test safari_webdriver)\n```\n\nThese tests cover bundled driver selection, Technology Preview capabilities, common/real/CLI routing, cookie conversion, cleanup, setup diagnostics and typed unsupported operations. The macOS `Safari WebDriver` workflow exercises local-page commands, HttpOnly cookie seeding, windows/tabs, screenshots and state isolation in a fresh session, with a separate runner for each language. All three language smokes passed on commit `1c7c484` ([macOS run](https://github.com/link-foundation/browser-commander/actions/runs/37505100619)).\n\nLocal validation: JavaScript **1,603 passed, 1 skipped**; Python **1,208 passed, 13 skipped**; Rust all-feature unit/integration tests and **20 doc tests passed**. JavaScript lint/format/duplication, Python Ruff/format/mypy, Rust fmt/Clippy, file-size checks, shared catalogue consistency, generated documentation checks and npm audit passed. Browser integration tests requiring installed browsers are opt-in; this Linux workspace cannot run Safari, so real Safari verification runs in macOS CI. The opt-in Rust Chrome storage-state integration also passed locally, transferring cookies and localStorage across Chromiumoxide, Playwright and Puppeteer in both launch modes.\n\nThe initial security run [37496961064](https://github.com/link-foundation/browser-commander/actions/runs/37496961064) failed on `GHSA-pqg4-j6r4-53mv` (`shell-quote` 1.10.0); the updated lockfile audit reports zero vulnerabilities. Investigation notes and commands are in `experiments/issue-126/`.\n\nThe first macOS run exposed Safari’s empty initial URL; reproducing JS/Python regressions verify that all native launchers initialize `about:blank` before restoring state. A later JS smoke exceeded its 60-second limit without identifying the stalled command. Timestamped phase diagnostics were added; the subsequent [JS smoke](https://github.com/link-foundation/browser-commander/actions/runs/37505100619/job/112411629948) passed all commands and cleanup in 37.5 seconds with the same timeout. A Chrome startup timeout in a separate parity run did not reproduce in the local integration test or in the [latest CI storage-state check](https://github.com/link-foundation/browser-commander/actions/runs/37505100755). These intermittent failures remain documented for investigation if they recur.\n\nFinal CI on commit `1c7c484`: **all 11 workflows passed**, including JavaScript/Python/Rust platform matrices, real Safari smokes, Chrome parity, package builds, Rust coverage and security checks. The branch includes the latest `main` and the working tree is clean.\n\n## Safari constraints\n\nSafari requires macOS and explicit one-time authorization. Its automation windows do not share the normal Safari profile; reuse sign-in by explicitly seeding importer cookies. Headless mode, persistent profiles, custom browser flags/preferences, CDP/BiDi, managed downloads, network interception, tracing and PDF are unavailable. See [setup, API examples and the capability matrix](https://github.com/link-foundation/browser-commander/blob/issue-126-f7c151d328c8/docs/safari-webdriver.md).\n\n<!-- hive-mind:changes:start -->\n### Changes\n- 53 file(s) modified\n- 2048 line(s) added\n- 109 line(s) removed\n- Files:\n  - `.github/workflows/safari.yml`\n  - `README.md`\n  - `docs/feature-parity.md`\n  - `docs/feature-parity/features.json`\n  - `docs/safari-webdriver.md`\n  - `experiments/issue-126/README.md`\n  - `js/.changeset/safari-webdriver.md`\n  - `js/package-lock.json`\n  - `js/src/browser/browser-sources.json`\n  - `js/src/browser/launcher.js`\n  - `js/src/browser/real-browser.js`\n  - `js/src/browser/safari-launch.js`\n  - `js/src/browser/safari-support.js`\n  - `js/src/browser/storage-state.js`\n  - `js/src/browser/webdriver.js`\n  - `js/src/cli/sessions.js`\n  - `js/src/core/webdriver-page.js`\n  - `js/src/exports.js`\n  - `js/src/traces/recorder.js`\n  - `js/tests/e2e/safari.e2e.test.js`\n  - `js/tests/unit/browser/real-browser.test.js`\n  - `js/tests/unit/browser/safari.test.js`\n  - `js/tests/unit/browser/webdriver.test.js`\n  - `js/tests/unit/cli/dispatcher.test.js`\n  - `python/changelog.d/126.added.md`\n  - `python/src/browser_commander/__init__.py`\n  - `python/src/browser_commander/browser/__init__.py`\n  - `python/src/browser_commander/browser/browser-sources.json`\n  - `python/src/browser_commander/browser/launcher.py`\n  - `python/src/browser_commander/browser/real_browser.py`\n  - `python/src/browser_commander/browser/safari_webdriver.py`\n  - `python/src/browser_commander/browser/storage_state.py`\n  - `python/src/browser_commander/core/engine_adapter.py`\n  - `python/src/browser_commander/exports.py`\n  - `python/src/browser_commander/traces/recorder.py`\n  - `python/tests/e2e/test_safari.py`\n  - `python/tests/unit/browser/test_safari_webdriver.py`\n  - `rust/changelog.d/safari-webdriver.md`\n  - `rust/src/browser/browser-sources.json`\n  - `rust/src/browser/launcher.rs`\n  - `rust/src/browser/mod.rs`\n  - `rust/src/browser/real_browser.rs`\n  - `rust/src/browser/real_browser_result.rs`\n  - `rust/src/browser/safari.rs`\n  - `rust/src/browser/webdriver/adapter.rs`\n  - `rust/src/browser/webdriver/capabilities.rs`\n  - `rust/src/browser/webdriver/mod.rs`\n  - `rust/src/core/engine.rs`\n  - `rust/src/traces/bundle.rs`\n  - `rust/src/traces/page.rs`\n  - …and 3 more\n<!-- hive-mind:changes:end -->\n","created_at":"2026-10-06T16:35:53Z","updated_at":"2026-10-06T18:11:05Z","closed_at":"2026-10-06T18:11:00Z","merged_at":"2026-10-06T18:11:00Z","merge_commit_sha":"b24e4c55ebd94d4fe6ba849ad31a394f89ffa16c","assignees":[{"login":"konard","id":1431904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1431904?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard","html_url":"https://github.com/konard","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-foundation/browser-commander/pulls